  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 249 PM CDT Sun Jul 12 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge continues to dominate the upper level\npattern across the Plains and the Rockies. This has brought \nwidespread hot temperatures into the Northern Plains. The low \nlevel thermal ridge is centered across eastern Montana. This \nwill cause temperatures to warm across western North Dakota to \naround 106 to 109 degrees this afternoon with the central and \nnorthern half of the state seeing 100 to 105. The central and \neastern half of the state has dew points in the 60s to lower 70s\nleading to heat index values of 105 to 110. There is also a \nhigh chance of breaking record high temperature for Bismarck, \nDickinson, Williston, and Minot for today and tomorrow. Tonight \nlow temperatures are forecast to drop down around 70s \npotentially breaking record high low temperatures for the same\nlocations.\n\nHot temperatures will continue into the start of the week. The\nlow level thermal ridge will slide eastward as the upper high \ncenters over the Northern Plains. High temperatures Monday are \nforecast to be around 100 to 105 with the hottest spots being \nthe southwest and the south central. A cold front is forecast to\nsag across the northwest leading to high temperatures in the \n90s for Crosby. The upper level ridge will dampen this week \nacross the Canadian Prairies. This will lead to multiple waves \ntraversing across southern Saskatchewan and Manitoba. There are\nlow chances of showers and thunderstorms by the middle of the \nweek into the weekend across the northern half of the state. The\nupper level ridge will persist across the the Plains through \nthe weekend. 100 degree temperatures are forecast across the \nsouthern half of the state through the middle of the week. After\nthat, above normal in the upper 80s to upper 90s are forecast \nto persist into the weekend.",
